    <GaugingStation location="Tyddyn Gwladys" name="Mawddach" number="64010">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Velocity Area station; predominantly forested catchment, highly responsive.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Problems with scouring of bed from boulders and shale movements in flood events. Station destroyed during 2001 flood event. Bed has since thought to have remained relatively stable. High responsiveness and geographical location make site difficult to gauge particularly in high flows. Multiple peak flow ratings across period of record.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Velocity Area station with pitching strip 100m downstream of cableway that is used to stabilise rating curve at low flow. Station added to peak flows dataset in August 2024 (WINFAP Files v13).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Suspect data 2001-2004 following flooding event that destroyed station.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Highly responsive and largely natural.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Steep mountainous catchment with much bare rock. Predominantly forested.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">N</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Gauged above QMED." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Gauged above QMED but highest AMAX is a catastrophic event, unlikely to be within 30%." suitable="No" type="Pooling"/>
